    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d433">

                <pb facs="0553" n="543" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg543"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/7647: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-03T14:00:00+07:00">November 3, 1942—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 4—1:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1271. TF–71. To Secretary of Treasury from Adler. Re 1 of TF–63 of October
                        8.<anchor n="93" xml:id="d433-f1"/> At Dr. Kung’s suggestion, board has
                    requested General Secretary and myself to make a trip to northwest to
                    investigate possibility of Board’s opening an [office at] Lanchow which would
                    grant United States dollar cover for commercial imports from Russia. General
                    Secretary and I [are] leaving for Lanchow November 3 for about 2 weeks.
                    [Adler.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
